 ],
 "note": "One turn of 71 messages: a short user prompt and 70 assistant messages of 6000 bytes each made of U+0001, which JSON escapes to 6 bytes (about 36 KiB per serialized message, 420 KB of content). Recovering it by turn_id goes oldest first; reopening and following the open page's next goes newest first (pages of older messages, each listed oldest first). Each page stops before the message that would pass 50 messages, 256 KiB of content or 1 MiB serialized (the sum of its envelopes), so here the serialized bound cuts the pages. Each page continues with history{next} and the token from the previous history_end. The concatenated pages hold every message exactly once, in order, with no history_end saying end: true before the last one."
